From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:52:20 -0400
Subject: feat: an Appearance card -- window colour, Space colour strength, tab
 highlight

GitHub issue 45, its third idea. Settings gains an Appearance card after
Sidebar, browser-wide as density is. "Window colour" is Stedding's own,
a neutral grey, or the user's, with a colour well for each look, kept
light enough for dark text in the light look and dark enough for light
text in the dark. "Space colour strength" scales the active Space's tint
of the ground, from none to strong. "Tab highlight" scales the rows'
tints, translucent at Subtle in the light look and ringed with a hairline
at Strong. The look lives in process-wide values the colour mixer reads;
a change drops the cached colour providers and re-themes every window.
The command bar has a cycling row for each.

Why: GitHub issue 45; the owner said yes on 2026-10-27 and asked on
2026-11-01 for it to be built here.
Removable when: never as a feature; the row painter's hunk goes if
Chromium's vertical rows gain an outline of their own.
